          "block_content": "Suppose we are again in three dimensions, and the three planes in the row picture do not intersect. What can go wrong? One possibility is that two planes may be parallel. The equations  $ 2u + v + w = 5 $ and  $ 4u + 2v + 2w = 11 $ are inconsistent—and parallel planes give no solution (Figure 1.5a shows an end view). In two dimensions, parallel lines are the only possibility for breakdown. But three planes in three dimensions can be in trouble without being parallel.",
